Besides the \(3.5\sigma\) co-linearity cut, another quantity, \(\chi^{2}\), was calculated from values of protons' scattering angles as co-linearity analysis cross check with the purpose to further reduce the remaining background. It is estimated that about 1% of background events remained in the data sample after the \(3.5\sigma\) co-linearity cut was applied. The \(\chi^{2}\) variable is given by:

